---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../../components/SiteFooter.astro';
import ProductServiceJourney from '../../components/ProductServiceJourney.astro';
import { describeServiceHref } from '../../data/contact';
---
<Base title="Registry Stack products | Records, review, documents, notices" description="See how Registry Stack products fit a licensing service: records, staff review, digitally sealed PDF documents, notices and information checks you authorise.">
  <SiteHeader current="products" />
  <main id="main-content" tabindex="-1">
    <section class="hero hero-cover" aria-labelledby="products-title"><div class="hero-inner"><div class="hero-copy">
      <p class="eyebrow">Registry Stack products</p>
      <h1 id="products-title">Software that keeps records and connects the steps of your register service.</h1>
      <p class="hero-lead">The products keep records, send requests to your staff and connect the next steps. They cover records, reviews, documents, notices and information checks. Use the parts you need. Use them beside an application you already run or in a new service.</p>
      <div class="hero-actions"><a class="button button-primary" href="#service-example">See how the products fit together</a><a class="button button-secondary" href={describeServiceHref('Registry Stack products')}>Discuss your service</a></div>
    </div></div></section>

    <section class="section" id="service-example" aria-labelledby="service-title"><div class="section-inner">
      <div class="section-heading"><h2 id="service-title">See how the products work together in a licence renewal.</h2></div>
      <ProductServiceJourney />
      <nav class="service-paths" aria-label="Priority service areas"><p>Choose the service you need:</p><ul><li><a href="/solutions/licensing/">Licensing and professional registers</a></li><li><a href="/solutions/business-and-tax/">Business registers</a></li><li><a href="/solutions/agriculture-food-and-environment/">Agricultural registers</a></li></ul></nav>
    </div></section>

    <section class="section section-muted" id="connections" aria-labelledby="connections-title"><div class="section-inner">
      <div class="section-heading"><h2 id="connections-title">Connect the steps and keep the systems you already have.</h2><p>Your application can call the products directly. Add integration components when your service needs them.</p></div>
      <div class="connection-grid">
        <article><h3>Registry Coordinator runs calls and waits for reviews</h3><p>It runs reviewed sequences of product calls. These can include waits for a staff decision. Each product still checks the permissions for its own operation.</p><a class="inline-cta" href="https://docs.registrystack.org/start/coordinator/">Read the Coordinator documentation <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></article>
        <article><h3>Registry Adapter lets you keep your existing source of records</h3><p>It exposes configured operations over a system you already run. The source system keeps its records and its authority. The integration defines which operations are available.</p><a class="inline-cta" href="https://github.com/registrystack/registry-stack/blob/v0.46.0/products/adapter/CONSULTATION.md">Read the Adapter integration contract <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></article>
      </div>
      <p class="additional-parts">If your service includes appointments, <a href="https://docs.registrystack.org/start/scheduling/">Registry Scheduling</a> manages capacity and bookings. Where participating sources publish information-provider descriptions, <a href="https://docs.registrystack.org/start/discovery/">Registry Discovery</a> helps technical teams find them.</p>
    </div></section>

    <section class="section" id="evaluation" aria-labelledby="evaluation-title"><div class="section-inner adoption-grid">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">For implementers</p><h2 id="evaluation-title">Try an example that connects staff review to a notice.</h2><p>The tutorial connects a workflow, staff review and a notice sent through a mock provider. Use it to inspect the handoffs.</p><a class="inline-cta" href="https://docs.registrystack.org/tutorials/review-an-application-and-send-a-notice/">Follow the review and notice tutorial <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
      <div><p class="eyebrow">Implementation and operation</p><h2>Choose who delivers and runs your service.</h2><p>Your own team or a provider you appoint can build the service and run the software. Or we build it with you and run it for you. You agree the records, screens, sign-in, connections and responsibilities in a written implementation scope. We quote our hosting and operation separately.</p><a class="inline-cta" href="/pricing/#process">Read how implementation works <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div>
    </div></section>
  </main>
  <SiteFooter />
</Base>
<style>
  .service-paths { border-top: 1px solid var(--registry-rule); margin-top: 32px; padding-top: 20px; }
  .service-paths p { font-size: var(--type-base); color: var(--registry-body); margin: 0 0 8px; }
  .service-paths ul { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px 28px; list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; }
  .service-paths a { display: inline-block; padding: 8px 0; font-size: var(--type-base); }
  .connection-grid, .adoption-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 40px; }
  .connection-grid article { border-top: 2px solid var(--registry-blue); padding-top: 22px; }
  .connection-grid h3 { font-size: var(--type-subhead); }
  .connection-grid p, .adoption-grid p { font-size: var(--type-body-sm); }
  .additional-parts { border-top: 1px solid var(--registry-rule); margin: 30px 0 0; padding-top: 22px; font-size: var(--type-base); }
  .adoption-grid h2 { font-size: clamp(28px, 3.5vw, 40px); }
  @media (max-width: 760px) { .connection-grid, .adoption-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 32px; } }
</style>
